      <h1>Understanding ARM64 Android Builds</h1>
      <p class="lead">Why architecture-matched native binaries matter when compiling Android apps on a phone.</p>
      <p>
        Android build tools such as AAPT2 and JDK binaries must match the device's CPU architecture
        (commonly <code>aarch64</code> / ARM64) to execute natively without desktop x86 emulation overhead.
      </p>
